    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Metabolic syndrome:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " after diet and exercise, metformin or a thiazolidinedione may be useful."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Pioglitazone 15 or 30 mg PO daily (15 mg with NYHA I–II HF); titrate by 15 mg to max 45 mg daily. Max 15 mg with gemfibrozil or other strong CYP2C8 inhibitors."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " causes or worsens CHF; not recommended in symptomatic HF; starting it in NYHA class III–IV HF is contraindicated. Don't use with active bladder cancer; caution with prior bladder cancer, edema, or liver disease."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Fluid retention/peripheral edema (most with insulin) and weight gain, sometimes > 10 kg; can worsen HF. Fractures (more in women), macular edema. Pioglitazone: possible bladder cancer (data conflicting). Rosiglitazone: may raise risk of HF, angina, MI, stroke. Hypoglycemia mainly when combined with insulin or a sulfonylurea."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Gemfibrozil (strong CYP2C8 inhibitor) raises pioglitazone exposure about 3-fold. With insulin, cut the insulin dose 10–25% if hypoglycemia occurs."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Liver tests before starting; routine periodic LFTs not needed without liver disease. Check LFTs promptly for symptoms of liver injury; stop if ALT > 3× ULN. After starting or raising the dose, watch for weight gain, edema and HF signs. Regular eye exams."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Can promote weight gain; use judiciously at the lowest dose in people with obesity."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
